── UNKNOWN NAME ───────────────────────── E0211_misspelled_name.lt:1:49  [E0211]

Unknown name `cuont`:

  1 │ fn average(count: i64, sum: i64) -> i64 { sum / cuont }
    │                                                 ^^^^^

Check the spelling. A local is visible after its `let`, and an item of another
module is named through it, as `fs.exists` after `use std.fs`.

To fix it, write `count`:

  1 │ fn average(count: i64, sum: i64) -> i64 { sum / count }
    │                                                 ~~~~~
